{"seq":1,"at":"2026-09-17","kind":"imported","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0681"},"reason":"Article of the Quiztopia bank (written for card c057): researched and transcribed in September 2026, converted to the quiz platform on 2026-10-20.","by":"Quiztopia import","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/quiztopia/c057.json"},
{"seq":2,"at":"2026-10-20","kind":"edited","target":{"type":"article","id":"a0681"},"reason":"Rewritten by the merge to take in the printed cards' questions.","by":"merge science/chemistry","ref":"quiz-archive/runs/tp-ingest/decisions/science__chemistry.json","changes":[{"field":"bodyEn","diff":[["=",1108],["+","Even a colour can come down to one compound. The main pigment in almost all white paint today is titanium dioxide (TiO2), a brilliantly white, opaque and chemically stable powder. First mass-produced in 1916, it displaced the poisonous lead white of the old masters and the weaker zinc white, and it is now estimated to account for about two-thirds of all pigment made worldwide, colouring not only paint but also paper, plastics, toothpaste and sunscreen.\n\n"],["=",123],["+","\n| White paint | Titanium dioxide (TiO2) | main pigment |"]]},{"field":"bodyDe","diff":[["=",1036],["+","Sogar eine Farbe kann sich auf eine einzige Verbindung zurückführen lassen. Das Hauptpigment fast jeder weißen Farbe ist heute Titandioxid (TiO2), ein strahlend weißes, deckendes und chemisch beständiges Pulver. Seit 1916 in großen Mengen hergestellt, verdrängte es das giftige Bleiweiß der alten Meister und das schwächere Zinkweiß, und heute macht es schätzungsweise rund zwei Drittel aller weltweit erzeugten Pigmente aus – es färbt nicht nur Wandfarbe, sondern auch Papier, Kunststoffe, Zahnpasta und Sonnencreme.\n\n"],["=",111],["+","\n| Weiße Farbe | Titandioxid (TiO2) | Hauptpigment |"]]}]},
