{"seq":34,"at":"2026-10-22","kind":"printed","target":{"type":"wording","id":"w24614"},"reason":"Printed on publish-or-perish card pp-039, category 1; the card's own words are kept in cardText — \"[Earth Science] What is the most abundant gas in the Earth’s atmosphere?\nA. Oxygen\nB. Nitrogen\nC. Carbon dioxide\nAnswer: B. Nitrogen makes up about 78% of the air we breathe. Nitrogen is a crucial part of the nitrogen cycle, which is essential for sustaining life on Earth by converting nitrogen in the atmosphere into forms that plants and animals can use.\".","by":"merge art/architecture, art/design, art/painting, art/sculpture, belief/philosophy, belief/religion, belief/symbols, ear","ref":"quiz-archive/transcripts/publish-or-perish/pp-039.json","changes":[{"field":"en","new":"What is the most abundant gas in the Earth's atmosphere?"},{"field":"de","new":"Welches Gas kommt in der Erdatmosphäre am häufigsten vor?"},{"field":"origin","new":"printed"},{"field":"printed","new":{"source":"publish-or-perish","card":"pp-039","category":1}},{"field":"cardText","diff":[["+","[Earth Science] What is the most abundant gas in the Earth’s atmosphere?\nA. Oxygen\nB. Nitrogen\nC. Carbon dioxide\nAnswer: B. Nitrogen makes up about 78% of the air we breathe. Nitrogen is a crucial part of the nitrogen cycle, which is essential for sustaining life on Earth by converting nitrogen in the atmosphere into forms that plants and animals can use."]]},{"field":"fact","new":"f03402"}],"hash":"b24085e77aba"},
